\section*{Costs}
The total annual cost for incarcerating community supervision violators in 2021 is \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(total.vp21)}!. \newline

\noindent The total annual cost for incarcerating just those with technical violations in 2021 is \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(total.tvp21)}!. \newline

\noindent Below is a table of these costs by state (no imputation). Note that missing cells indicate that a state did not submit 2021 population data:

\begin{table}[h]
{\tiny \Sexpr{table_costs}}
\end{table}

\section*{Averted Costs}

The previous MCLC survey averted costs were calculated from pre-COVID looking at 2019-2020. These costs were \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(avert19_20last)}!. States were given the opportunity to make data corrections in this year's MCLC survey, and so the current averted costs looking at 2019-2020 are \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(avert19_20)}!. The difference is \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(avertdiff)}!. \newline

\noindent The 2019-2021 total averted costs: \verb!\Sexpr{dollar_format()(avert19_21)}!.

\end{document}